#NEXUS

[ harris2004a_fig4: Panel A, read by eye at 3-4x. Dicraeosauridae, Diplodocinae, Diplodocidae and Diplodocoidea, each joined to its node by an arrow, are kept as internal labels. Polytomies: the root (Theropoda and Prosauropoda meet the sauropod line at one point), Haplocanthosaurus-Diplodocoidea-Macronaria (two lines converge into that node), and the four-way titanosaur node (Nemegtosaurus, “Titanosaurus” colberti, Opisthocoelicaudia-Alamosaurus, Neuquensaurus-Saltasaurus). 29 tips, 3 polytomies (3, 3, 4 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 7 case (census 2, seed 20261241). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

